sliding-window.pseudo:
// Canonical variable window: atMost(target) for nonnegative array
function atMost(a, S):
    if S < 0: return 0
    left = 0; sum = 0; count = 0
    for right in 0 .. n-1:
        sum += a[right]
        while sum > S:           // restore invariant sum <= S
            sum -= a[left]; left += 1
        count += right - left + 1 // all subarrays ending at right
    return count

// exact-sum count = atMost(S) - atMost(S-1)
// min-length     = shrink while sum >= target, track right-left+1
// fixed-k max    = window width pinned to k, O(1) add/evict, score when full

